! TEMPLATE: Restrained Membrane Minimization
! DESCRIPTION: Minimize solvent/lipid tails with protein and lipid phosphorus restrained
! TYPE: minimization
! PRIORITY: 1
! AUTHOR: ProPrep (based on packmol-memgen protocol)
! VERSION: 1.0

Restrained energy minimization of the membrane-protein system. Protein residues
and lipid phosphorus atoms (@P31) are positionally restrained with 10 kcal/mol*Å^2
to relax water, ions, and lipid tails while maintaining bilayer structure and
protein conformation. 5000 steepest descent + 5000 conjugate gradient cycles.

&cntrl
! Run Control
  imin = 1,			! Energy minimization (0=MD, 1=minimization)
  maxcyc = 10000,		! Maximum minimization cycles
  ncyc = 5000,			! Steepest descent cycles before switching to conjugate gradient

! Input_Output Control
  ntx = 1,			! Read coordinates, but not velocities
  ntpr = 100,			! Every ntpr steps, print human-readable energy info
  ntwx = 0,			! No trajectory output during minimization

! Restraints
  ntr = 1,				! Enable positional restraints
  restraint_wt = 10.0,			! Restraint force constant (kcal/mol-A2)
  restraintmask = '(!:WAT,Na+,Cl-,K+,Cs+ & !@H=) | @P31',	! Non-solvent heavy atoms + lipid phosphorus

! Miscellaneous
  nmropt = 0,
  cut = 10.0,			! Nonbonded interaction cutoff (Angstroms)
/

